at 480 0
door 0 32 1 2
flag carrying_pib
flag pib_home
quest stolen_pib The Stolen Pib
stage Find the baby pib the goblins carried off into the north.
stage Bring the baby pib back to the merchant at the caravan.
dialog merchant
line root
say Well met, traveller.
ask Show me your wares. -> grief
need flag pib_home off
ask Show me your wares. -> end
need flag pib_home on
gets trade
ask You look troubled. What happened? -> trouble
need quest stolen_pib unstarted
ask I have your baby pib. -> thanks
need flag carrying_pib on
ask Farewell. -> end
line grief
say Forgive me. My baby pib is gone, and grief has left no room in me for trade. I will open my wares to no one until it is home.
ask What happened to it? -> trouble
need quest stolen_pib unstarted
ask Farewell. -> end
line trouble
say Every night the goblin camp up the north road sends raiders down on us, a few at a time until dawn. My guards hold the carts, but last night one slipped past them and carried off my baby pib. Will you bring it back to me?
ask I will find it. -> accepted
gets quest stolen_pib stage 1
ask That is not my problem. -> end
line accepted
say Bless you. Their camp lies up the north road, past the carts.
line thanks
say My little one! You have my thanks, traveller. Stay near my guards after dark; the raiders still come down every night.
act flag carrying_pib off
act flag pib_home on
act quest stolen_pib done
dialog baby_pib
line root
say A baby pib, tied to a stake. It squeaks at you.
ask Untie it and carry it home. -> end
gets flag carrying_pib on
gets quest stolen_pib stage 2
ask Leave it. -> end
dialog home_pib
line root
say The baby pib nuzzles the merchant's boots.
dialog cook
line root
say Mind the pot. If you're hungry you're too late, and if you're early you're in the way.
ask What's cooking? -> pot
ask How long has the caravan been on the road? -> road
ask Farewell. -> end
line pot
say Whatever the guards shot yesterday, and turnips the merchant swears are worth their weight in silver. Don't repeat that.
ask Farewell. -> end
line road
say Since the thaw. Down from the hill towns, along the Strand, and now camped at this bridge with goblins at our backs and the Fenwood in front. Nobody wants to cross that river.
ask Why not? -> fen
ask Farewell. -> end
line fen
say Ask the warden on the bridge. He's seen what comes out of those trees. I only cook for the ones who come back.
dialog drover
line root
say Careful round the carts. The axles are older than I am and twice as cranky.
ask What's in the crates? -> crates
ask Seen anything strange? -> strange
ask Farewell. -> end
line crates
say Salt, rope, lamp oil, nails. The sacks are grain, mostly. Nothing worth dying over, though the goblins don't seem to know that.
ask Farewell. -> end
line strange
say Lights past the river after dark, low over the water. The warden says it's their cookfires. I've never seen a cookfire that moves.
dialog captain
line root
say Keep your blade sheathed inside the camp. My guards have had a long week.
ask The raids? -> raids
ask Could you use another sword? -> help
ask You heard about the baby pib? -> pib
need quest stolen_pib done
ask Farewell. -> end
line raids
say Every night, a few at a time, down the north road. We hold the carts; we can't hold the dark. If you're staying, stay near the carts.
ask Farewell. -> end
line help
say Always. Clear that goblin camp up north and the raids stop. Until then I'll take any blade that points the right way.
ask Farewell. -> end
line pib
say I heard. One of my guards let it past him, so I owe you twice. The merchant hasn't stopped smiling since.
dialog warden
line root
say Hold there. Past this bridge the road runs into the Fenwood, and the Fenwood is no place for a lone traveller.
ask What's in the Fenwood? -> fen
ask Who holds it? -> camps
ask I can handle myself. -> brave
ask I'll turn back. -> end
line fen
say Trees grown so thick you lose the sky by noon, and water on every side. Leeches in the shallows. Worse than the goblins up north, and they're bad enough.
ask Who holds it? -> camps
ask Farewell. -> end
line camps
say Cutthroats. They've dug in behind rings of water with a plank across to each camp, and they shoot whatever comes over the plank. Shieldmen, crossbows, netters. Not the rabble that raids the carts.
ask I can handle myself. -> brave
ask Farewell. -> end
line brave
say Then I won't stop you. But if you come back over this bridge running, don't expect me to hold it for you.
